[2026-03-04T21:15:58.724Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013a4pHbpL5AXbmctGCGLRXg","type":"tool_result","content":"# Key Instructions for Using Replay CLI for Debugging\n\n## Quick Setup\n1. **Install**: Run `npm i -g replayio` (or use yarn/pnpm/bun)\n2. **Authenticate**: Get an API key from https://app.replay.io settings and set it as the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable\n\n## Recording Workflow\n- Launch a recording session with `replayio record [url]` to start the Replay Browser\n- The tool \"launches Replay Browser and starts recording the given URL\"\n- Stop recording by closing the browser\n\n## Upload & Manage\n- Use `replayio upload [ids...]` to submit recordings for analysis\n- List all local recordings with `replayio list`\n- Remove unwanted recordings via `replayio remove [ids...]`\n\n## Debugging Integration\n- Access the Replay MCP Server to \"debug your recorded application\" by configuring it with your API key\n- The server integrates with Claude for enhanced debugging capabilities\n\n## Additional Commands\n- `replayio info` - Check CLI and browser versions\n- `replayio login/logout` - Manage account access\n- `replayio help` - View all available commands\n\nThis workflow enables systematic capture and analysis of application behavior for effective debugging."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"52368737-6ec8-4ea8-bd8c-d8bae0c12160","uuid":"087f58c4-7c23-4fe3-99e5-a1045d4e973c","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4854,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Key Instructions for Using Replay CLI for Debugging\n\n## Quick Setup\n1. **Install**: Run `npm i -g replayio` (or use yarn/pnpm/bun)\n2. **Authenticate**: Get an API key from https://app.replay.io settings and set it as the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable\n\n## Recording Workflow\n- Launch a recording session with `replayio record [url]` to start the Replay Browser\n- The tool \"launches Replay Browser and starts recording the given URL\"\n- Stop recording by closing the browser\n\n## Upload & Manage\n- Use `replayio upload [ids...]` to submit recordings for analysis\n- List all local recordings with `replayio list`\n- Remove unwanted recordings via `replayio remove [ids...]`\n\n## Debugging Integration\n- Access the Replay MCP Server to \"debug your recorded application\" by configuring it with your API key\n- The server integrates with Claude for enhanced debugging capabilities\n\n## Additional Commands\n- `replayio info` - Check CLI and browser versions\n- `replayio login/logout` - Manage account access\n- `replayio help` - View all available commands\n\nThis workflow enables systematic capture and analysis of application behavior for effective debugging.","durationMs":3413,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-cli/SKILL.md"}}
[2026-03-04T21:15:59.332Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01J7jqDetqSSUN7djeXEF9ps","type":"tool_result","content":"# Key Instructions for Using Replay MCP for Debugging\n\n**Structured Investigation Approach:**\nFollow a methodical four-step process: formulate a specific question, explore relevant events in the recording, explain why those events occurred, and support conclusions with gathered data.\n\n**Primary Tool Categories:**\n\n1. **Exploratory Tools** - Discover what happened and when:\n   - Error tracking (uncaught exceptions, React errors)\n   - Timeline analysis (console messages, network requests, React renders)\n   - Source code inspection (find files, read code, search patterns)\n\n2. **Explanatory Tools** - Understand causation:\n   - \"Dependencies track happens-before relationships between events\" to clarify why things occurred\n   - Stack frames and control flow analysis\n   - Point-specific details (variables, DOM state, component trees)\n\n**Practical Debugging Strategy:**\nLocate code relevant to your question, verify whether it executed, then use the Logpoint tool to examine expression values across execution points. For timing issues, trace dependencies backward from the problem event to identify what triggered it and any associated delays.\n\n**Core Principle:** Avoid jumping to conclusions—use systematic exploration and concrete data to validate hypotheses rather than assumptions."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"52368737-6ec8-4ea8-bd8c-d8bae0c12160","uuid":"100bc5d6-2248-44f8-a99f-d6e3fbdd406d","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4555,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Key Instructions for Using Replay MCP for Debugging\n\n**Structured Investigation Approach:**\nFollow a methodical four-step process: formulate a specific question, explore relevant events in the recording, explain why those events occurred, and support conclusions with gathered data.\n\n**Primary Tool Categories:**\n\n1. **Exploratory Tools** - Discover what happened and when:\n   - Error tracking (uncaught exceptions, React errors)\n   - Timeline analysis (console messages, network requests, React renders)\n   - Source code inspection (find files, read code, search patterns)\n\n2. **Explanatory Tools** - Understand causation:\n   - \"Dependencies track happens-before relationships between events\" to clarify why things occurred\n   - Stack frames and control flow analysis\n   - Point-specific details (variables, DOM state, component trees)\n\n**Practical Debugging Strategy:**\nLocate code relevant to your question, verify whether it executed, then use the Logpoint tool to examine expression values across execution points. For timing issues, trace dependencies backward from the problem event to identify what triggered it and any associated delays.\n\n**Core Principle:** Avoid jumping to conclusions—use systematic exploration and concrete data to validate hypotheses rather than assumptions.","durationMs":3535,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-mcp/SKILL.md"}}
